{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpkAhtwbwJYD65QoabtA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Not directly.** A deploy restarts every Durable Object instance on the new code. In-flight requests get a short grace period, and WebSocket connections are dropped, even hibernated ones. There's no setting that keeps an object on old code for a set amount of time.\n\nThe closest option is **gradual deployments**. Run `wrangler versions upload`, then `wrangler versions deploy` with a percentage split, such as 90% old and 10% new. Each Durable Object runs only one version at a time, and which version it gets is decided by its object ID. So most objects stay on the old code until you raise the new version's percentage. Objects still restart when they switch over.\n\nEither way, build for restarts. Keep important state in Durable Object storage rather than in memory, and have clients reconnect WebSockets automatically."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2258,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2258},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8fa1a104-08cb-4068-b41d-dbd25df130d1","uuid":"933b567b-f5f5-487f-b6f2-13ad1d73dc11","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:09:33.459Z","request_id":"req_011CfpkAheoaCD9cY9pwL1ef"}
